[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopResource.cs" id="1_shop"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopStockEntry.cs" id="2_entry"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ShopInvestmentTier.cs" id="3_tier"]

; Bryn's forge (Phase 38E). The second merchant in the game, and the first one reached by talking to a
; person rather than by a dev command: Bryn keeps his conversation and his quest, and trade hangs off a
; DialogueEffect.OpenShop choice on his root node.
;
; What he deals in is the whole of his identity until 38F gives shops real specialties. Materials over
; gear, deliberately:
;   - Ingots, strips and scrap are UNLIMITED (Quantity = 0). A smith who runs out of stock bar turns
;     crafting into a shopping trip, and there is nothing interesting about being told to come back
;     tomorrow for iron.
;   - Finished gear is FINITE and thin — one sword, one vest, two caps. DESIGN §6 is explicit that gold
;     buys convenience and gear but never the defining power, and a shelf the player can shop off
;     competes with loot and crafting for the same job. Three days is long enough that the sword is an
;     event rather than a supply line.
;
; RestockDays = 2 (slower than Aldreth's daily turnover — a forge works through its stock, a stall
; restocks from a cart). It is also what makes the finite rows and the purse legal: --validate rejects
; finite stock or a positive purse on a shop with no clock, because the first is emptied by the first
; player through the door and the second never refills.
;
; SellFraction 0.45 sits above Aldreth's 0.4: a smith knows what metal is worth, so scrap and ore go
; further here than at the general stall. That is the first time in the game two merchants have paid
; differently for the same item, and it is the seed of 38F's specialist premium. It stays far below
; BuyMarkup — equal or inverted is an infinite gold loop, and both the validator and ShopPricing clamp it.
;
; PurseGold 300: enough to fence a good haul, not enough to fence a field of corpses in one visit. It
; refills with the shelves on the same two-day clock.
;
; No LeveledTable on purpose. Aldreth's rolled pool is the game's one leveled shelf; a second one halves
; how special it is and doubles the chance the player just shops until something Legendary appears.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Stock_ingot"]
script = ExtResource("2_entry")
ItemId = "item.material.iron_ingot"
Quantity = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Stock_strips"]
script = ExtResource("2_entry")
ItemId = "item.material.leather_strips"
Quantity = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Stock_scrap"]
script = ExtResource("2_entry")
ItemId = "item.material.scrap"
Quantity = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Stock_sword"]
